            <ArticleTitle>Case report: intussusception--a cause of chronic abdominal symptoms and weight loss.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>723-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A chronic clinical course for intussusception of the bowel in children is an unusual, but well recognized phenomenon. We report a case of a young child whose symptoms of vomiting and abdominal pains continued for over a month before radiological investigation made the diagnosis of ileocolic intussusception which was then successfully reduced by air enema.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
